#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Texas
#> pause: 50
#> must: Iowa is west of Ohio.
#> must: Texas
#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: <b>
#> not: <a
#> source: //ba
# 27. Remove HTML tags, even ones split over lines. Pement: sed -e :a -e 's/<[^>]*>//g;/</N;//ba'
# <[^>]*> is "< then anything but > then >": a whole tag, removed everywhere
# on the line by g. If a < is still left, the tag continues on the next line:
# N appends it and // (the same pattern, <) sends the loop back to a. The
# sheet's quote-a-message entries,  s/^/> /  and  s/^> // , work the same way.
# Try: delete the  /</N;//ba  and see the broken tag survive.
:a
s/<[^>]*>//g;/</N;//ba

#DATA
<b>Iowa</b> is <i>west</i> of <a
href="ohio.html">Ohio</a>.
<p>Texas</p>
